# Love Me Do, verse (figure 21.2)
# Thirteen bars: the two-bar unit G-C sung three times with three lines of words (2+2+2), then
# seven bars on "please ... love me do" and the harmonica hook. Pollack lines the words up with the
# beat counts he types above each bar; he says he has removed the syncopation of the singing.
# The harmonica comes back in the second bar of the third system ("Resume harmonica hook ...")
# and carries through the "..." bars; he types no notes for it, so none are added here.
#? The harmonica hook (F-E-D-G, per the intro discussion) could be drawn in mm. 9-13, but Pollack gives no rhythm or placement for it here.
key G

system
caption 3X
words           | 1 2 3 4 | 1 2 3 4 |
words           | Love,*2 love me | do.*3 You |
words           | know*2 I love | you.*3 I'll |
words           | al-*2 ways be | true*3 So |
